      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n\n// Fast integer reading using getchar_unlocked (thread-unsafe but fast)\nstatic inline int read_int() {\n    int x = 0;\n    char c = getchar_unlocked();\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar_unlocked(); // skip whitespace\n    bool neg = false;\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar_unlocked(); }\n    do {\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        c = getchar_unlocked();\n    } while (c > ' ');\n    return neg ? -x : x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = read_int();\n    int s = read_int();\n\n    const int np1 = n + 1; // size of prefix sum dimension (extra row/col of zeros)\n    std::vector<long long> pref(np1 * np1, 0LL);\n\n    // First pass: read matrix and compute horizontal prefix sums in one go\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        const int base_i = (i + 1) * np1;\n        #pragma ivdep\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int val = read_int();\n            row_sum += val;\n            pref[base_i + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Second pass: vertical accumulation to complete the integral image\n    long long *pref_ptr = pref.data();\n    #pragma ivdep\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const int base_cur = (i + 1) * np1;\n        const int base_prev = i * np1;\n        long long * __restrict__ cur_row = &pref_ptr[base_cur];\n        const long long * __restrict__ prev_row = &pref_ptr[base_prev];\n        #pragma ivdep\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            cur_row[j + 1] += prev_row[j + 1];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using blocking to improve cache reuse\n    const int B = 64; // block size tuned for L1 cache\n    long long mxSum = -9223372036854775807LL - 1; // LLONG_MIN\n\n    for (int ii = 0; ii < n - s + 1; ii += B) {\n        const int i_end = std::min(ii + B, n - s + 1);\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < n - s + 1; jj += B) {\n            const int j_end = std::min(jj + B, n - s + 1);\n            #pragma ivdep\n            for (int i = ii; i < i_end; ++i) {\n                const long long * __restrict__ row_i_s = &pref_ptr[(i + s) * np1];\n                const long long * __restrict__ row_i   = &pref_ptr[i * np1];\n                #pragma ivdep\n                for (int j = jj; j < j_end; ++j) {\n                    long long sum = row_i_s[j + s] - row_i[j + s]\n                                   - row_i_s[j] + row_i[j];\n                    if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining fast integer parsing integrated with horizontal prefix sum construction eliminates separate matrix storage, reducing memory traffic. Using a smaller block size (B=64) improves L1 cache reuse of integral image data during submatrix search. Adding restrict pointers and ivdep pragma enables compiler auto-vectorization.",
